  "term": "simple structure",
  "definition": "In this historical passage, a simple structure is a bodily or sensory arrangement thought of as a single, undivided mechanism. The term is used in contrast to a more complex structure, such as a nerve-fibre regarded as made up of smaller fibrils that might support more than one kind of excitation.",
